def find(d,text):
 a=[p for p in d.paragraphs if text in p.text];assert len(a)==1,(text,len(a));return a[0]
def replace(d,old,new):
 a=[r for p in d.paragraphs for r in p.runs if old in r.text];assert len(a)==1,(old,len(a));a[0].text=a[0].text.replace(old,new);a[0].font.highlight_color=WD_COLOR_INDEX.YELLOW
def after(a,text,style=None):
 e=OxmlElement('w:p');a._p.addnext(e);p=Paragraph(e,a._parent);p.style=style or a.style;p.add_run(text).font.highlight_color=WD_COLOR_INDEX.YELLOW;return p
def before(a,text,style='Normal'):
 e=OxmlElement('w:p');a._p.addprevious(e);p=Paragraph(e,a._parent);p.style=style;p.add_run(text).font.highlight_color=WD_COLOR_INDEX.YELLOW;return p
m=Document(PRE/'Manuscript_comment6_revised.docx')
replace(m,'Yield results varied with system and comparator; a common-test analysis gave an average improvement for Fe(P7)Cl but not for the Fe(CMC-Por)Cl aryl cohort.','Yield results varied with system and comparator; a common-test analysis gave an average improvement for Fe(P7)Cl but not for the Fe(CMC-Por)Cl aryl cohort. A committee-disagreement baseline had lower mean ee prediction error than PULSE-Acquire in both datasets.')
a=find(m,'For a paired-endpoint analysis, the common-test splits')
after(a,'To compare established selection approaches, the same ee splits and starting pairs were used for query by committee, expected improvement and Thompson sampling. The committee selects the largest disagreement among the existing three predictive models; expected improvement and Thompson sampling use a fixed Gaussian-process surrogate on Morgan/Tanimoto fingerprints to maximise observed ee. All routes were evaluated using the same held-out Ridge predictor and budgets; three seeded Thompson continuations per starting pair were averaged. Optimisation and prediction-error objectives are distinct (SI Section S14).')
a=find(m,'In the repeated common-test analysis, the mean paired')
after(a,'In the established-method comparison, mean held-out ee MAE for uncertainty–diversity / query by committee / expected improvement / Thompson sampling was 13.88 / 13.22 / 13.56 / 14.27 for Fe(P7)Cl and 14.27 / 13.99 / 15.15 / 15.65 for Fe(CMC-Por)Cl aryl substrates. Query by committee had lower mean error in both datasets, and expected improvement did so for Fe(P7)Cl. The overlapping-split results vary by test set and evaluate specific fixed implementations; they do not establish a state-of-the-art ranking. Because the latter two methods target high ee, the best observed ee is also reported in the SI (Section S14).')
replace(m,'The acquisition advantage was neither estimator- nor endpoint-universal, and common-test yield results differed between the two systems.','The acquisition advantage was neither estimator- nor endpoint-universal; common-test yield results differed between systems, and committee disagreement gave lower mean ee error in both benchmark datasets.')
m.save(P/'Manuscript_comment7_revised.docx')
s=Document(PRE/'Supporting_Information_comment6_revised.docx');a=find(s,'Declaration of AI-assisted manuscript preparation')
before(a,'S14 Established active learning benchmark','Heading 1')
before(a,'We compared uncertainty–diversity with query by committee (QBC), expected improvement (EI) and Thompson sampling (TS) using the 20 overlapping common-test ee splits, three starting pairs and label budgets 2, 6, 10, 15 and 20 described in Section S8. The same candidate pools, held-out sets and seven-record Fe(CMC-Por)Cl audit exclusion apply. QBC chooses the largest standard deviation of the clipped predictions from Ridge, Elastic Net and Tanimoto-kNN. It uses the same model-disagreement component present in the uncertainty–diversity score, without its novelty and coverage terms. QBC is represented here by this particular heterogeneous committee (Burbidge, Rowland and King, IDEAL 2007, DOI: 10.1007/978-3-540-77226-2_22).')
before(a,'EI and TS use the same Gaussian-process surrogate on Morgan-fingerprint Tanimoto similarities, fitted separately to revealed |ee| labels at every step. Training labels were centred and divided by their population standard deviation (scale 1 ee point if zero); the kernel has fixed diagonal noise variance 0.05 in standardised units, with no hyperparameter optimisation. EI selects the largest expected improvement over the best revealed ee with zero exploration offset. TS selects the maximum of a correlated joint sample from the latent posterior over the remaining candidates, using three seeded continuations per start and small numerical jitter. These are fixed implementations of optimisation methods, not exhaustively tuned baselines (Frazier, arXiv:1807.02811; Bijl et al., arXiv:1604.00169).')
before(a,'All routes were scored with the same 1,287-field Ridge predictor on the held-out records. MAEs were averaged over five budgets, three starts and, for random and TS, three continuations before averaging over 20 splits. The PULSE, source and random paths and predictions were reused from Section S8. Mean ee MAEs for PULSE / QBC / EI / TS / source / random were 13.88 / 13.22 / 13.56 / 14.27 / 16.72 / 14.25 for Fe(P7)Cl, and 14.27 / 13.99 / 15.15 / 15.65 / 15.70 / 15.33 for Fe(CMC-Por)Cl aryl. PULSE gave lower error than QBC in 8/20 splits in each system, than EI in 7/20 and 15/20, and than TS in 11/20 and 14/20, respectively. At budget two all routes have identical predictions because their initial pairs are shared.')
before(a,'EI and TS aim to find high ee rather than minimise held-out error. At six labelled substrates, mean best revealed |ee| for PULSE / QBC / EI / TS / source / random was 93.53 / 93.48 / 93.38 / 93.65 / 92.83 / 93.41% for Fe(P7)Cl and 84.92 / 86.72 / 85.37 / 86.73 / 87.83 / 87.01% for Fe(CMC-Por)Cl aryl. Best values use only acquired labels and are retrospective measurements on the available pool; they are not prospective gains in experimental effort. Complete per-budget values, predictions, paths, seeds, hashes and implementation checks are retained in the accompanying records.')
before(a,'QBC gave lower mean common-test error than PULSE in both datasets; EI also did so for Fe(P7)Cl. PULSE and QBC share committee predictions, and GP acquisition uses a fingerprint surrogate whereas all routes share the Ridge evaluation model. The small related datasets, overlapping splits, three TS runs, fixed GP choices and absence of prospective validation prevent population-level significance or a state-of-the-art ranking. These results compare specified implementations and do not show general superiority of PULSE over established acquisition approaches.')
a.paragraph_format.page_break_before=True;s.save(P/'Supporting_Information_comment7_revised.docx')
